PREAMBLE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

EE ZONE was built out of a genuine belief that engineering education should be
accessible to every student — regardless of whether they can afford expensive
software licenses or attend a well-funded institution.

This license reflects that belief. It is written to be human-readable first,
legally sound second. If you are a student, a teacher, or someone who just
wants to learn electrical engineering — you are welcome here, unconditionally.

If you are a company or individual seeking to profit from this work, this
license asks only one thing in return: give credit where it is due.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 1 — DEFINITIONS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

"The Software"       refers to the EE ZONE platform — all source code, assets,
                     scripts, database schemas, documentation, configuration
                     files, and any derivative works contained in this
                     repository.

"The Author"         refers to Ajinkya Chalke, the original creator and sole
                     copyright holder of this Software.

"You" / "Licensee"   refers to any individual, organization, institution, or
                     automated system that accesses, downloads, copies, forks,
                     modifies, deploys, or otherwise interacts with this
                     Software.

"Educational Use"    means use by students, self-learners, academic
                     institutions, non-profit training organizations, open
                     workshops, and educators — for learning, teaching, or
                     research purposes — where no direct revenue is generated
                     from the Software itself.

"Commercial Use"     means any use where the Software, or a substantial portion
                     of it, is used to generate direct or indirect revenue,
                     including but not limited to: SaaS products, paid courses,
                     enterprise internal tools, consulting deliverables, or
                     white-labelled platforms.

"Derivative Work"    means any modification, adaptation, translation, port,
                     or extension of the Software that incorporates a
                     substantial portion of its source code or architecture.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 2 — GRANT OF RIGHTS FOR EDUCATIONAL USE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Subject to the conditions in Section 4, the Author grants You a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual license to:

  ✦  Use the Software for personal learning and skill development
  ✦  Study the source code to understand engineering platform architecture
  ✦  Fork and modify the Software for academic projects and coursework
  ✦  Deploy the Software for classroom demonstrations or university labs
  ✦  Share the Software freely within educational communities
  ✦  Build upon the Software for open-source, non-commercial tools

This grant is FREE, unconditional in intent, and requires no written
permission from the Author — as long as Section 4 (Attribution) is followed.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 3 — COMMERCIAL USE TERMS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Commercial Use of this Software is permitted ONLY under the following
conditions — ALL of which must be satisfied simultaneously:

  3.1  ATTRIBUTION DISPLAYED
       The original author (Ajinkya Chalke) must be visibly credited in the
       application UI, product documentation, marketing materials, and any
       public-facing about page or footer.

  3.2  NO WHITE-LABELLING WITHOUT PERMISSION
       You may not remove, obscure, or replace the original authorship
       attribution with your own branding and present the Software as if
       you created it. Any public commercial deployment must retain a visible
       link to the original repository.

  3.3  AI FEATURES ARE NON-TRANSFERABLE
       The AI-powered modules of this platform (Instrument Scanner, Problem
       Solver, AI Circuit Designer, AI Code Assistant, AI Troubleshooter)
       may not be extracted, repackaged, and sold as standalone commercial
       AI products without explicit written permission from the Author.

  3.4  NOTIFICATION ENCOURAGED
       While not legally required, the Author kindly requests that you send
       a brief message to ajinkyachalke008@gmail.com if you deploy this
       Software commercially. This helps the Author understand the platform's
       real-world impact.

  If you cannot meet the above conditions, you must obtain a separate
  commercial license by contacting the Author directly.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 4 — ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY FOR ALL USE)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

This is the ONE non-negotiable condition that applies to every Licensee,
whether educational or commercial:

  4.1  SOURCE CODE
       All copies or substantial portions of the Software — including forks,
       mirrors, and derivative works — must retain this license file and the
       following copyright notice at the top of the primary README or
       equivalent documentation:

         "Originally created by Ajinkya Chalke — github.com/ajinkyachalke008"

  4.2  DEPLOYED APPLICATIONS
       Any public web deployment of this Software or a Derivative Work must
       display the following in a visible location (footer, about page, or
       credits section):

         "Powered by EE ZONE — Built by Ajinkya Chalke"
         (with a link to: github.com/ajinkyachalke008/EEZONE-08)

  4.3  ACADEMIC PUBLICATIONS
       If this Software is referenced in a thesis, research paper, or academic
       publication, please cite it as:

         Chalke, A. (2025). EE ZONE: AI-Powered Electrical Engineering Platform.
         GitHub. https://github.com/ajinkyachalke008/EEZONE-08

